{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/pulls/7","id":4134232019,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTVpH8872a1_T","html_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/7","diff_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/7.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/flowercomputers/bogkit/pull/7.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/flowercomputers/bogkit/issues/7","number":7,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"add MUDGarden, a persistent gardening MUD built on Fold","user":{"login":"dnbrwstr","id":357216,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzIxNg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/357216?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr","html_url":"https://github.com/dnbrwstr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnbrwstr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nMUDGarden is a persistent gardening MUD over SSH. Human players and model-planned residents share one serialized world and the same command, permission, and mutation paths.\n\nThis is a BogKit hackathon submission in the agent support and novel interface\n/ gaming categories.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Adds the complete `examples/mudgarden` crate and documentation.\n- Uses Fold to persist the keyed world source and incrementally maintain actors, rooms, gardens, plants, schedules, ecology, species aggregates, and moisture percentiles.\n- Adds SSH play, a browser field console, multi-player test sessions, editable content, resident action traces, Docker packaging, and Railway configuration.\n- Updates `Cargo.lock` for the new example dependencies.\n\n## How did I test?\n\n- `cargo test --locked -p mudgarden` — 63 passed\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p mudgarden --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo fmt --package mudgarden --check`\n- `bash -n examples/mudgarden/scripts/*.sh`\n- `docker build --check --file examples/mudgarden/Dockerfile .`\n\n## Hackathon submission\n\n### category\n\n- [x] agent support\n- [ ] performance\n- [x] novel interface / gaming\n\n### team\n\n- **project name:** MUDGarden\n- **team / author name(s):** Daniel Brewster\n- **contact (optional):** via this PR\n\n### what you built\n\nA persistent shared gardening world where plants, weather, ecology, people, and autonomous residents continue changing between connections. Fold is the source of truth and incrementally maintains the materialized views that make world reads, due schedules, ecological stress, spatial lookups, and aggregate statistics cheap.\n\n### how to run\n\n```bash\n# from repo root\n./examples/mudgarden/scripts/run-mudgarden.sh\nssh -p 2222 <name>@127.0.0.1\n```\n\nSet `OPENAI_API_KEY` to enable model-planned residents. The world simulation and human play work without it. The browser field console opens at `http://127.0.0.1:2223`.\n\n### demo / notes\n\nThe field console shows the live room graph, 8x8 gardens, global habitat grid, organisms, Fold-derived schedules and aggregates, event history, and inspectable resident action traces.\n\n### checklist\n\n- [x] i forked bog-kit and built my project in this fork\n- [x] my project is runnable from this pr\n- [x] i selected both applicable categories\n- [x] this pr is my official hackathon submission acknowledgment\n","created_at":"2026-07-25T22:56:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T13:52:33Z","closed_at":"2026-08-16T13:52:33Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"627e2